## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_xform2d.html
- Summary (EN): Applies a 2D transformation to a height layer and can also scale and offset the height values themselves.
- Résumé (FR) : Applique une transformation 2D à une couche de hauteur, avec mise à l'échelle et décalage optionnels des valeurs de hauteur.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the height layer to transform"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Units", "meaning": "space in which translations are measured: image, texture, pixel or local"}, {"name": "Transform Order", "meaning": "order in which the transformations are applied"}, {"name": "Translate, Rotate, Scale, Shear, Uniform Scale", "meaning": "the 2D transform, rotation in degrees about the pivot"}, {"name": "Pivot Translate", "meaning": "moves the local pivot used for the transform"}, {"name": "Invert Transformation", "meaning": "applies the inverse, so matching nodes cancel each other"}, {"name": "Apply Transform Scale to Height", "meaning": "scales height pixels along with the 2D transform"}, {"name": "Grid Scale", "meaning": "stretches or contracts the layer horizontally"}, {"name": "Height Scale", "meaning": "stretches or contracts the height values vertically"}, {"name": "Height Offset", "meaning": "shifts the height values up or down"}]

- Caveats: ["Height Scale and Height Offset change the height values, not just the layer position.", "The page does not say how Transform Order interacts with the height settings."]

